WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.421
The method is tested across several settings.

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:08.922
On CIFAR-10 as the in-distribution data,

00:00:09.002 --> 00:00:13.423
SVHN serves as a far out-of-distribution set and
CIFAR-100 as a harder near out-of-distribution set.

00:00:13.503 --> 00:00:17.924
The authors also study misclassification prediction
on CIFAR-10 and scale up to ImageNet-1K

00:00:18.004 --> 00:00:22.426
with ImageNet-O as the out-of-distribution set.

00:00:22.506 --> 00:00:26.927
Notably,

00:00:27.007 --> 00:00:31.428
DAB works with a very narrow eight-dimensional
latent bottleneck and just ten distributional codes,

00:00:31.508 --> 00:00:35.929
and is compared against strong baselines including
deep ensembles, DDU, DUQ, DUE,

00:00:36.009 --> 00:00:40.430
SNGP, and the vanilla variational Information Bottleneck.
